.TH MELBAND-ROFORMER 1 "2026-09-24" "melband-roformer 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
melband-roformer \- separate vocals/speech from music using Mel-Band RoFormer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B melband-roformer
.RI [ INPUT.wav " | " GLOB " ...]"
.RB [ \-\-output\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-device
.BR auto | cuda | cpu ]
.RB [ \-\-model
.IR SLUG ]
.br
.B melband-roformer
.BR \-\-info | \-\-self\-test | \-\-list\-models | \-\-download\-model | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B melband-roformer
is a Debian-packaged CLI wrapper around the upstream
.B melband-roformer-infer
project (MIT licensed), providing local, offline, GPU-accelerated
vocal/instrumental music source separation using the Mel-Band RoFormer
architecture. No audio is sent to any network service.
.PP
Given one or more input audio files (WAV/FLAC/MP3/OGG, anything
.BR libsndfile / ffmpeg
can decode), it writes
.IR NAME _vocals.wav
and
.IR NAME _instrumental.wav
for each input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-dir " DIR"
Directory to write output files to (default: current directory).
.TP
.BI \-\-device " auto|cuda|cpu"
.B auto
(default) uses the NVIDIA GPU via CUDA if available, otherwise CPU, and
prints which it chose.
.B cuda
forces GPU use and exits with an explanatory error (not a Python
traceback) if CUDA is unavailable.
.B cpu
forces CPU even if a GPU is present.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " SLUG"
Select a model from the upstream registry (default:
.BR melband-roformer-kim-vocals ,
the recommended MelBand Roformer Kim model by Kimberley Jensen). See
.BR \-\-list\-models .
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-path " FILE" ", " \-\-model\-path " FILE"
Bypass registry auto-resolution and use an explicit local config/checkpoint
pair.
.TP
.BI \-\-models\-dir " DIR"
Override the model cache directory (default:
.IR ~/.cache/melband\-roformer\-infer/ ).
.TP
.B \-\-yes ", " \-y
Assume "yes" to the model-download confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-info
Print Python/PyTorch/CUDA/GPU/model diagnostic information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Run a full readiness check: Python, PyTorch, CUDA, GPU, model presence,
model loading, and a small real inference pass. Prints
.BR [OK] / [FAIL] / [SKIP]
per check.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-models
List all models available in the upstream registry, with category and
description.
.TP
.B \-\-download\-model
Download (with confirmation and sha256 verification) the selected
.RB ( \-\-model )
or default model, then exit without processing any audio.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the application version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/melband-roformer-infer/<model-slug>/
Downloaded model checkpoints and configs (upstream's own default cache
location; not managed by dpkg).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/melband-roformer/venv/
Bundled, isolated Python environment (PyTorch, upstream package, and this
wrapper). Not intended for direct use.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure (forced GPU unavailable, download declined, self-test
found a problem, separation subprocess failed).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (bad arguments, missing input file, unknown model slug).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Basic:
.RS
.EX
melband-roformer song.wav
.EE
.RE
.PP
Batch, explicit output directory, forced GPU:
.RS
.EX
melband-roformer ./input/*.wav --output-dir ./output --device cuda
.EE
.RE
.SH KNOWN LIMITATIONS
Mel-Band RoFormer is trained primarily on sung vocals, not spoken word.
Extracting a short spoken monologue from a music intro (e.g. an
industrial-track intro) often works reasonably but is
.B not guaranteed
to be clean; result quality depends heavily on the specific mix. Always
listen to the output.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation:
.IR /usr/share/doc/melband-roformer/README.md ,
.IR /usr/share/doc/melband-roformer/README.debian.md .
Upstream project: https://github.com/openmirlab/melband-roformer-infer
.SH AUTHOR
Packaged for Debian 13 (Trixie) as part of this deliverable; wraps
third-party upstream code and models, see
.IR /usr/share/doc/melband-roformer/copyright .
